{"id": "tea:adipurana-jinasena:16", "source": "src:adipurana-jinasena", "location": {"ref": "16"}, "paraphrase": "Ṛṣabha, as the first king when the wish-fulfilling trees failed, taught the six means of livelihood — arms, writing, agriculture, learning (or arts), trade and crafts — and ordered society into kṣatriyas, vaiśyas and śūdras by occupation.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:rsabha"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-time-cycle"], "notes": "Parvan 16 (moderate confidence).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:adipurana-jinasena:38", "source": "src:adipurana-jinasena", "location": {"ref": "38"}, "paraphrase": "Bharata, wishing to honour the virtuous among the laity, had grass sprouts strewn on the path to his palace; those who would not walk on the living sprouts he made the brāhmaṇas (dvija), invested with the sacred thread as a mark of their vows, and taught them the life-cycle rites (kriyā) of the Jain householder.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "narrative"], "teachers": ["tch:bharata-cakravartin"], "concepts": ["cpt:jain-brahmana"], "disputes": ["dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "notes": "Parvans 38–40 (moderate confidence). See brw:dharmasastra-samskaras-to-jain.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:adipurana-jinasena:ch.4", "source": "src:adipurana-jinasena", "location": {"ref": "ch.4", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Some foolish men say a creator made the world; but if he made it, where was he before, what material did he use, and why would a perfect being create a world of suffering? The world is uncreated, like time, without beginning or end, made of the substances.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:no-creator-jain", "cpt:loka-purusa"], "teachers": ["tch:jinasena"], "disputes": ["dsp:isvara"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Chapter 4 of the Ādipurāṇa (verse range c. 16–40 recalled); arguments given in substance.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
